## What was wrong

In `src/paginate.ts`, the slice start was `page * perPage`, so page 1 skipped the first `perPage` items — every list started at the second page.

## Changes

**`src/paginate.ts`**
- Start index is now `(page - 1) * perPage`, so page 1 begins at index 0.
- Throws `RangeError` when `page < 1` or `perPage < 1`.
- No explicit empty-page handling is needed: a page past the end makes `slice` start beyond the array length, which returns `[]` naturally. Same for `perPage` only items per page, leaving the last partial page intact.

**`src/paginate.test.ts`**
- Added tests importing `paginate`: page 1 returns the first `perPage` items; subsequent pages continue where the previous left off (page 3 of 7 items / 3-per-page returns just `[7]`); a page past the end returns `[]`; page 1 of an empty list returns `[]`; page below 1 throws `RangeError`; perPage below 1 throws `RangeError`.

